678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,2679,400,71,7021,11730,59,67,37018,90,16,43010,15170,17,12034,31716,11,1221,1128,374,279,897,315,400,71,87210,16,25547,20,15087,30,17399,697,4226,304,44548,1352,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIf $h(y)=\\dfrac{1+y}{2-y}$, then what is the value of $h^{-1}(5)$? Express your answer in simplest form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"543e7ca27866f9a0b68da469985107c25bf26f686630f79cfcbf93837c51947b"},"seconds":7.612368822097778,"seed":51716365426298186,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the value of \\( h^{-1}(5) \\), we need to determine the value of \\( y \\) such that \\( h(y) = 5 \\). Given the function \\( h(y) = \\dfrac{1+y}{2-y} \\), we start by setting \\( h(y) = 5 \\) and solving for \\( y \\).\n\n1. Set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\dfrac{1+y}{2-y} = 5\n   \\]\n\n2. Clear the fraction by multiplying both sides by \\( 2-y \\):\n   \\[\n   1 + y = 5(2 - y)\n   \\]\n\n3. Distribute the 5 on the right side:\n   \\[\n   1 + y = 10 - 5y\n   \\]\n\n4. Combine like terms by adding \\( 5y \\) to both sides:\n   \\[\n   1 + 6y = 10\n   \\]\n\n5. Isolate the term with \\( y \\) by subtracting 1 from both sides:\n   \\[\n   6y = 9\n   \\]\n\n6. Solve for \\( y \\) by dividing both sides by 6:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{9}{6} = \\frac{3}{2}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( h^{-1}(5) \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:640"}
